# Spec for tools/riscpkg.py: ReelEdit.
Package: ReelEdit
Section: Video
Priority: Optional
Licence: Free
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Standards-Version: 0.4.0
Environment: arm32, vfpv3
Depends: SharedUnixLibrary (>= 1.16), ARMEABISupport
Components: Apps.Video.!ReelEdit (Movable LookAt)
Homepage: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-reeledit
Description: Non-linear video editor, built on MLT and FFmpeg
 Cut, trim, move, split and roll clips; fades, dissolves and wipes; a
 clip's colour and looks, pan and zoom, special effects, freeze frames
 and countdowns; sound clean-up, levels, loudness and audio tracks;
 logos, picture in picture (with keyframes), green screen and titles in
 RISC OS fonts; slow, fast and reverse motion; render previews and
 proxies; autosave. Exports MP4 (H.264 and AAC) with the Pi's VideoCore
 encoder, typed as a video (&FB2). Needs a Raspberry Pi 2, 3 or 4;
 gpu_mem=128 for 1080p. The User Guide is inside (F1).
 .
 This is a beta (Beta 2).
Build-Map: !ReelEdit -> Apps/Video/!ReelEdit
Build-Notice: ReelEdit, packaged for PackMan from the release zip on
 https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-reeledit/releases
 .
 ReelEdit is free software under the GNU GPL version 2 or later. It
 contains MLT, FFmpeg with x264, ReelHWAccel, libxml2 and others; as a
 whole it is distributed under the GPL version 2. The licences, and
 where each part's source is, follow.
